{title: The LORD, He Is God}
{subtitle: 1 Kings 18:20–39}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | ×14

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Ahab called all Israel up to Carmel's height
Four hundred fifty prophets came to win the fight
One man stood before them with the peo[C#]ple standing [F#]round
[G#m]Two bulls on the wood and not [D#m]a spark upon the ground
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
How long will you keep limping [C#]between two o[D#m]pinions
If the LORD is God, follow him
[C#]The god who answers with fire, he is [D#m]God
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
From morning until noon they called on [C#]Baal by [F#]name
[D#m]They danced around their altar [C#]but no answer [F#]ever [D#m]came
They cut themselves with swords and [C#]spears until the eve[F#]ning [G#]hour
No sound, no answer, no response, no fire and [D#m]no power
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Elijah took twelve stones, one for each [C#]tribe of Jacob's [F#]sons
He [D#m]built the LORD an altar where the bro[C#]ken one had [F#]come
[D#m]Fill four jars with water, pour it out [C#]on wood and [F#]stone
[G#]Do it a third time, till the trench is overflown
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[D#m]Answer me, LORD, [C#]answer me
[D#m]So that this people may [C#]know that you, LORD, are [D#m]God
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Then the fire [B]of the LORD [F#][C#]fell
And con[D#m]sumed the [B]burnt offering, [F#]the wood, the stones, [C#]and the [D#m][B][F#]dust
And it [C#]licked up the [D#m]water in the [B]trench
[F#]The LORD, he is [C#]God
The LORD, [D#m]he [B][F#]is [C#]God
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The LORD, [D#m]he is [B][F#][C#]God
The [D#m]LORD, [B][F#]he [C#]is [D#m][B][F#][C#]God
{end_of_verse}

